```text id="snakepattern01"
Time Limit: 1 sec
Memory Limit: 256 MB

Description

Draw a snake pattern on an n × m table.

The tail of the snake starts at (1,1) and moves right to (1,m).
Then it moves 2 rows downward to (3,m).
Next, it moves left to (3,1).
From there it moves 2 more rows downward to (5,1), and the pattern continues.

Empty cells are represented by '.' and snake cells by '#'.

Input Format

A single line containing two integers n and m.

Output Format

Print n lines, each containing m characters, representing the snake pattern.

Constraints

3 ≤ n, m ≤ 50
n is an odd number.

Sample Input 1
5 6

Sample Output 1
######
.....#
######
#.....
######

Sample Input 2
3 4

Sample Output 2
####
...#
####

Sample Input 3
7 3

Sample Output 3
###
..#
###
#..
###
..#
###

Note

The snake pattern alternates between:

- Rows completely filled with '#'.
- Rows containing a single '#' at either the left or right end.

Specifically:
- Every odd-numbered row is filled entirely with '#'.
- Among the even-numbered rows:
  - The 2nd, 6th, 10th, ... rows have '#' in the last column.
  - The 4th, 8th, 12th, ... rows have '#' in the first column.

This creates the continuous snake path described in the statement.
```


#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
typedef long long ll;
#define endl "\n"   // optional, better to avoid redefining endl

void solve() {
    int n,m;
    cin>>n>>m;

    bool flag = false;
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
{
    if(i % 2 == 0)
    {
        for(int j = 0; j < m; j++)
        {
            cout << "#";
        }
    }
    else
    {
        for(int j = 0; j < m; j++)
        {
            if(flag == false)
            {
                if(j == m - 1)
                    cout << "#";
                else
                    cout << ".";
            }
            else
            {
                if(j == 0)
                    cout << "#";
                else
                    cout << ".";
            }
        }

        flag = !flag;   // move here
    }

    cout << endl;       // move here
}
}

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int t = 1;
    //cin >> t;
    while (t--) {
        solve();
    }

    return 0;
}
